<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abdel Fattah el-Sisi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1954">1954</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abdel Fattah el-Sisi is an Egyptian army officer who has been president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> since 2014. As defence minister and head of the armed forces he led the removal of President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohamed-morsi">Mohamed Morsi</a> in July 2013, after which security forces crushed the Muslim Brotherhood, killing hundreds at Rabaa Square. His rule has been marked by large state building projects and severe repression of dissent.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abdel-fattah-el-sisi.jpg" alt="Abdel Fattah el-Sisi" width="320" height="402" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ministry of Communications and Information Technology in Egypt · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AbdelFattah_Elsisi_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
